 DM_SAVE_SYNC	player	Cloud saves: the folder whose `<title ID>/save.dmsync` the save is synced through, `icloud` for iCloud Drive/nxnative Saves (the Mac); `0` or unset, off. The Mac launcher sets the folder chosen in its settings window's Cloud saves, the iPhone app the one picked in its launcher (dm/host/save_sync.h); regress.py, bench.py and the NSP script's own host runs set `0`
 DM_SAVE_SYNC_CHOICE	switch	Cloud saves: set by a front end that asks the player when the cloud's save and this device's both changed (any value: a save that changed on both sides is replaced on neither without a choice); `ask`: no choice yet, `cloud:<hash>` brings in the cloud's save with that hash, `local:<hash>` sends this device's over the cloud's save with that hash (`local:none`: the cloud had none), `offline`: the cloud could not be read before the start, so the host does not wait for it; unset, the newer save wins (dm/host/save_sync.c, docs/frontends.md)
