-DM_SCREEN_ASPECT	player	`=<width/height>` (1.3 to 1.77, e.g. `1.6` for MacBook 16:10, `1.43` for the iPhone Duo) renders a build with installed screen-shape stubs in that shape: output 1920 wide, 1280-wide layout space, the HUD at the taller edges and 16:9's sides in view; `auto` the app window's own shape (iOS) or the main screen's below its notch (Mac, with a window; the loader then leaves the variable holding the ratio or `0`) when it is taller than 16:9, else 16:9; `0` or unset is 16:9; launcher setting
+DM_SCREEN_ASPECT	player	`=<width/height>` (1.3 to 1.77, e.g. `1.6` for MacBook 16:10, `1.43` for the iPhone Duo) renders a build with installed screen-shape stubs, or a build with screen-shape stubs (Ocarina of Time, nxnative PR #3037), in that shape: output 1920 wide, 1280-wide layout space, the HUD at the taller edges and 16:9's sides in view; `auto` the app window's own shape (iOS) or the main screen's below its notch (Mac, with a window; the loader then leaves the variable holding the ratio or `0`) when it is taller than 16:9, else 16:9; `0` or unset is 16:9; launcher setting
 DM_SCREEN_ASPECT_SITES	diagnostic	`=<mask>` with DM_SCREEN_ASPECT: which of the profile's layout-size conversion stubs follow the taller layout, one bit each (default all)
